    {
      "id": "Q-MATH-POLY-HOTS-14",
      "stem": "If p(x) = 2x^4 - x^3 - 7x^2 + ax + b is divisible by x^2 - 2x - 3, find the value of a + b.",
      "source_ref": "HOTS Q14",
      "answer": {
        "kind": "MODEL_RESPONSE",
        "summary": "-34",
        "reasoning": [
          "Divisor factors: x^2 - 2x - 3 = (x - 3)(x + 1).",
          "Conditions: p(3) = 0 and p(-1) = 0.",
          "p(-1) = 2(1) - (-1) - 7(1) - a + b = 2 + 1 - 7 - a + b = -4 - a + b = 0 => b - a = 4.",
          "p(3) = 2(81) - 27 - 7(9) + 3a + b = 162 - 27 - 63 + 3a + b = 72 + 3a + b = 0 => 3a + b = -72.",
          "Solving gives a = -19, b = -15 => a + b = -34."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "Q-MATH-POLY-SA-6",
      "stem": "Without calculating cubes, evaluate 48^3 - 30^3 - 18^3.",
      "source_ref": "SA Q6",
      "answer": {
        "kind": "MODEL_RESPONSE",
        "summary": "77760",
        "reasoning": [
          "Let a = 48, b = -30, c = -18. Then a + b + c = 48 - 48 = 0.",
          "Therefore, 48^3 + (-30)^3 + (-18)^3 = 3(48)(-30)(-18) = 3 * 48 * 540 = 77,760."
        ]
      }
    },
